-- title:
--   Existence of the classifying map to a universal deformation ring
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a commutative local ring with finite residue field $k=\mathrm{ResidueField}\,\mathcal O$, let $\bar\rho$ be a residual Galois representation over $k$ (a $k$-space of rank $2$ with a monoid homomorphism from $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)$ to its endomorphisms that is trivial on the fixers of some finite extension of $\mathbb Q$ inside $\overline{\mathbb Q}$), and let $\mathcal D$ be a predicate on rank-two adic Galois representations over local $\mathcal O$-algebras satisfying [`GaloisRep.IsDeformationCondition`](def/GaloisRep_DeformationCondition.html#L19): invariance under equivalence, stability under base change along local $\mathcal O$-algebra maps between Artinian test algebras, descent along injective such maps, descent along fibre products, and, over complete Noetherian local $\mathcal O$-algebras with surjective residue map, equivalence with holding after every surjection onto an Artinian test algebra. Let $\rho_0$ be a continuous homomorphism to $\mathrm{GL}_2$ of the discrete residue field object, and $b$ a basis of $\bar\rho$'s space with $\rho_0\sigma$ the matrix of $\bar\rho(\sigma)$ in $b$ for all $\sigma$. Let $R$ be a local pro-Artinian $\mathcal O$-algebra whose topology is the $\mathfrak m_R$-adic one, together with a corepresentation datum $e$ exhibiting $R$ as corepresenting the quotient subfunctor [`Deformation.conjQuotSubfunctor`](def/Deformations_ConjQuotSubfunctor.html#L22) of [`GaloisRep.conditionSubfunctor 𝒪 𝒟 ρ₀`](def/GaloisRep_ConditionLifts.html#L22), whose value on an object $A$ consists of the classes of those continuous $\rho'\colon\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)\to\mathrm{GL}_2(A)$ lifting $\rho_0$ such that $\mathcal D$ holds for every rank-two representation over an Artinian object $B$ with $A\to B$ whose matrices in some basis are the pushforward of $\rho'$, classes being taken modulo conjugation by elements of $\mathrm{GL}_2(A)$ reducing to $1$. Let $\rho^{u}\colon\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)\to\mathrm{GL}_2(R)$ lie in that set of lifts, have class equal to the element of the functor attached by $e$ to $\mathrm{id}_R$, and induce an adically continuous action on $R^2$ (hypothesis `hcont`). Finally let $A$ be a Noetherian local ring, complete for its maximal-ideal-adic topology, an $\mathcal O$-algebra with local structure map whose composite with the residue map $A\to \mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ is surjective, and let $\rho_A$ be a rank-two adic Galois representation over $A$ with $\mathcal D(\rho_A)$ whose residual representation is equivalent to the base change of $\bar\rho$ along $k\to\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$. Then there is a local $\mathcal O$-algebra homomorphism $\varphi\colon R\to A$ such that the base change along $\varphi$ of the representation $(R^2,\rho^{u})$ is equivalent to $\rho_A$.
--
--   This is the existence half of Mazur's universal property for a ring corepresenting the deformation functor of framed lifts of type $\mathcal D$: every lift of type $\mathcal D$ over a complete Noetherian local $\mathcal O$-algebra with residue field generated by $\mathcal O$ arises by base change from the universal one, with no uniqueness of $\varphi$ asserted. It feeds [`GaloisRep.nonempty_deformationRingData`](thm.html#GaloisRep.nonempty_deformationRingData), which packages the universal deformation ring together with its universal property for later use.
